**Given:**

dfrac{b}{a} = 0.75

**Formula used:**

Substitute dfrac{b}{a} = 0.75 into the expression dfrac{2a - b}{2a + b} + dfrac{8}{9}

**Calculation:**

b = 0.75a

⇒ dfrac{2a - 0.75a}{2a + 0.75a} + dfrac{8}{9}

⇒ dfrac{1.25a}{2.75a} + dfrac{8}{9}

⇒ dfrac{125}{275} + dfrac{8}{9}

⇒ dfrac{5}{11} + dfrac{8}{9}

⇒ dfrac{45 + 88}{99}

⇒ dfrac{133}{99}

∴ The correct answer is option (1).
